      "id": 2,
      "options": {
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "Storage quota by storage class.\n\n- **Hard (usable) GB** — the logical quota granted to the namespace; this is what counts against your PVC requests.\n- **Used GB** — logical GB currently consumed against that hard quota.\n- **Raw (replicated) GB** — physical Ceph capacity actually reserved, after replication overhead: `Raw = Hard × Replication`.\n- **Replication** — how many physical copies Ceph keeps per logical GB on that storage class.\n\n| Storage class | Replication | Used for | Why choose it |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `ocs-storagecluster-ceph-rbd-virtualization` | 3× (3-site) | OpenShift **VM disks** only | Not for end-user/application storage — reserved for virtualization workloads |\n| `ocs-storagecluster-ceph-rbd` | 3× (3-site) | **General-purpose** container storage | Default choice for most application PVCs needing full 3-site resilience |\n| `ocs-storagecluster-ceph-non-resilient-rbd` | 1×, not replicated | Apps with their **own replication**, e.g. Kafka, Elasticsearch | Minimizes physical storage usage — no Ceph-side redundancy, since the app already replicates data itself |\n| `ceph-rbd-2-site` | 2×, 2-site | **General-purpose**, smaller footprint | Cheaper than 3-site RBD when full 3-site resilience isn't required |\n| `ocs-storagecluster-cephfs` | 3× (3-site) | Shared **filesystem (ReadWriteMany)** access | Use when multiple pods need concurrent read/write to the same volume |\n\n**Choosing between them:** default to `ocs-storagecluster-ceph-rbd` for general application PVCs; use `ceph-rbd-2-site` when you want a smaller replication footprint and can accept 2-site resilience; use `ocs-storagecluster-ceph-non-resilient-rbd` only for workloads that replicate data themselves (Kafka, Elasticsearch) to avoid paying for redundant Ceph replication; use `ocs-storagecluster-cephfs` only when you need shared multi-pod filesystem access; never request `ocs-storagecluster-ceph-rbd-virtualization` for application/container storage — it's reserved for OpenShift Virtualization VM disks.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "13.3.0-32457798232",
      "title": "How to read this table",
      "type": "text"
    },
